## Learn About Your Rights Oxnard Lemon Law Claims

Oxnard - located west of Los Angeles - is no stranger to heavy traffic. To make matters worse, some SoCal drivers are navigating the roads in defective vehicles: known as lemons. Lemons are cars that were not manufactured properly - and have one or more problems that impair its safety, value, or functionality.

Lemons do not discriminate. In California, anyone with a new, used, or leased vehicle can end up with a lemon. That’s why the Song Beverly Consumer Warranty Act (California lemon law) was put into effect.

As an Oxnard lemon law attorney, I help consumers understand the legal process in California and help them get the compensation they deserve.

If your vehicle meets the criteria below, you may be eligible for benefits.

- The vehicle manufacturer has made at least two or more attempts to repair a warranty-covered defect, or

- The vehicle has been out of service for more than 30 days while being repaired for warranty-covered problems; and

- The vehicle has several warranty-covered problems, which were not caused by abuse of the vehicle and that impair its use, value, or safety.

