If you have a lemon - with the warranty still in effect - you need to file your claim ASAP. Get in touch with a lemon law attorney in Oxnard to start the process.

The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty. As long as the defect is reported to the manufacturer within the terms of the original warranty, your claim is valid.

If your vehicle meets the criteria of California lemon law, your Oxnard lemon law attorney will fight for:

