## Oxnard, California Lemon Law and Used Cars

Did you know used vehicles can qualify for benefits under lemon law in California?

Did You Buy a Defective Used Car from an Auto Dealership?

The used car can be processed like new if you bought it with a warranty or an implied warranty of merchantability - and it’s still in effect.

Learn Your Used Car Lemon Law Rights

Per California lemon law, dealerships must cover the repair costs and provide a replacement/buyback. The warrantor will cover the legal fees.

Did You Buy the Vehicle “As Is”?

According to California law, the “as is” clause MUST be showcased prior to purchase. Your rights indicate you may not be eligible for benefits if you bought the car “[as is](/blog/avoid-buying-a-car-as-is-from-a-dealership).”

